{
  "changelog": "method-structure-diagnostic v1.0.0 \u2014 Initial release\n\n- Provides a structured diagnostic tool for assessing the completeness and coherence of Method sections in psychology research papers.\n- Evaluates according to 11 core structural dimensions, strictly referencing standard checklists, rubrics, and top-journal exemplars.\n- Outputs a detailed, fixed-format report with scoring breakdown, core issues, targeted improvements, and sample excerpts from exemplary papers.\n- Ensures consistent, objective scoring with transparent justification, and enforces tight boundaries regarding scope and collaboration with other evaluation skills.\n- Integrated logic for exemplar usage; supports actionable, prioritized revision recommendations.",
